      "identity": "Setup Factory trojan wrapper bundling Huorong plus an encrypted EXE/import-proxy DLL",
      "evidence": [
        "Reverse-engineered the native launcher archive parser (0x401233), engine reconstruction (0x4014ce), Lua DLL extraction (0x4015e0), and shell launch (0x401b8c). XOR-7 applies only to the first 2000 engine bytes.",
        "Recovered irsetup.dat and the two final application stages using LZMA. On Post Install contains two Shell.Execute calls: one starts the Huorong NSIS package and the other starts B11CWynFd.exe.",
        "B11CWynFd.exe carries a PerformanceToolX64 publisher/PDB identity but has invalid Authenticode image digest and near-random encrypted .text. Its sole imported module is hLzpZBD.d, through 123 renamed mixed-case API imports; the EXE entry bytes do not decode as ordinary executable code.",
        "hLzpZBD.d is an unsigned DLL with a Fabrikam/Vertex placeholder identity, randomized exports that satisfy the EXE imports, only LocalAlloc/LocalFree imports, and opaque control-flow arithmetic in an added executable section. Followed entry call 0x180002080 to 0x1805d8ce5 and its protected dispatcher.",
        "An inert Unicorn run of DLL entry reached LocalAlloc and protected module/header traversal, then faulted in the incomplete mock loader environment. No native sample code, requested OS actions, or network calls were executed. Final payload functionality remains unresolved.",
        "x2PhI6L5.T is a valid 230x180 PNG. Concatenated IDAT has 10,856,414 bytes after the completed zlib image stream. The bytes are opaque; no static claim that this data is activated is made.",
        "The Huorong repair executable statically includes real curl implementation, SHA-256 Windows patch support and crash-dump APIs. The signed sysdiag driver has legitimate kernel termination APIs. Those facts are not evidence of fake curl payload loading, credential theft or defender killing.",
        "Verified all 123 imports in B11CWynFd.exe occur among the 212 sidecar exports; this is a connected import-proxy pair, not unrelated files."
      ],
