      "judgment_context": "Likely malicious: default-project wrapper launches a publisher-signed program whose code/import interface was replaced and an opaque disguised sidecar is loaded. Genuine bundled security software does not authorize those modifications. Operator, delivery pretext and final payload purpose are unknown.",
      "coverage_limits": [
        "The automatic scan visits 160 carved Huorong/support members but does not recover the Setup Factory LZMA application members or post-install script. The new host-proxy and retained opaque-DLL findings only fire after manual extraction.",
        "Original classifier after correction says benign (level -1, probability 0.9133495). Both recovered malicious stages also have level -1 despite a hostile YAML finding. This is a classifier miss; no false trait was restored to raise a score.",
        "Two distinct hostile findings cover the manually extracted EXE proxy and opaque DLL. The 3-5 goal is unmet: the post-install activation and surplus PNG data are established manually, but the relevant decoded members are absent from the original report. Existing YAML byte/string matchers do not decompress arbitrary LZMA. A Lua Shell.Execute pair by itself also cannot distinguish a malicious wrapper from an ordinary installer.",
        "DLL protection prevented resolving final network, injection, persistence or theft behavior. Those actions were not invented to satisfy the trait target. The emulator failure is a limitation, not evidence of successful payload execution."
      ]
